{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfXVeR77dU5VLNVLW379y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both deliverables are written and the budget is spent down to 0.5 credits.\n\n**Answer:** Q1 0.635, Q2 -0.065, Q3 HOLD. Model B should not replace A.\n\n**What I found.** The LLM judge and expert review both put B ahead of A by 5 to 7 points. Full verification says the reverse. B's responses are 3 to 4 times longer than A's. For B responses under 900 tokens, review matched verification perfectly. Above that, verification failed most review-passed responses, dropping to a 0.34 pass rate between 1500 and 2200 tokens and zero above 2200. For A, review matched verification on all 33 checked responses, including the 8 longest, so A's review pass rate of 0.700 stands as its verified rate.\n\n**How the estimate was built.** I spent 120 credits on expert review of all 1200 responses, 306 on verifying 153 B responses stratified by length, 66 on verifying 33 A responses, and 7.5 on a crowd probe that turned out too noisy to use. For B, verified verdicts are used directly, review fails count as zero, and unverified review passes are weighted by a logistic fit of verification pass probability against log length. A three-band lookup gives the same Q1 within 0.001. The bootstrap interval for Q1 is 0.62 to 0.65, well inside the 0.02 tolerance.\n\nThe report at `/app/report.md` documents the purchases, the length table, and a note that both the judge and time-boxed review systematically over-credit long responses."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1552,"cache_read_input_tokens":39534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1552,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":504,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"310293c2-9254-43fb-be74-5a321